<title>SPAIN: BANK OF SPAIN LEAVES KEY MONEY RATE AT 5.25 PCT.</title>
<headline>BANK OF SPAIN LEAVES KEY MONEY RATE AT 5.25 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain said it left its key money rate unchanged at 5.25 percent at Thursday's regular repurchase tender for central bank certificates.</p>
<p>It allotted 3.04 trillion pesetas ($19.6 billion) against 3.06 trillion bid.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160 ($ = 154.9 Spanish Pesetas)</p>
